course: dictionary
lesson: 9460
title: Starfish: an animal that is not a fish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A starfish is a sea animal shaped like a star, usually with five arms. It lives on the sea floor and on rocks. «Most starfish have 5 arms with a simple eye at the tip of each.» The sentence tells you what the animal looks like, so you can picture it.
explain: Scientists also call it a sea star, because it is not a fish. This is a surprising clue, because the word starfish seems to say fish. «A starfish and a jellyfish are not fish at all, because they have no backbone and no gills.» Context helps you see that a word can mean something other than what it seems to say.
explain: Words can also be used to compare things. «Skydivers spread out like a starfish to catch more air» is not about the sea. Here starfish describes how a body looks with its arms and legs wide. When you meet a word in a new place, ask yourself: is this the animal, or is it a comparison?
fact: A starfish is a sea animal, not a fish.
fact: Scientists also call a starfish a sea star.
fact: Most starfish have five arms, and each arm looks like a point of a star.
fact: «Skydivers spread out like a starfish» uses the word to describe a shape.
fact: A starfish has no brain and no backbone, and it can slowly grow back a lost arm.
exercise: «A starfish and a jellyfish are not fish at all.» What is a starfish? | A type of sea shell | *A sea animal shaped like a star, often with five arms | A bright star seen from the sea | A small fish with a star on its tail
exercise: «Skydivers spread out like a starfish to catch more air.» What is starfish being compared to here? | A rock on the beach | A fish swimming fast through the water | A bird folding its wings | *The way a body looks with its arms and legs spread wide
exercise: Scientists say a starfish is also called a sea star. Why? | *Because it is not a fish | Because it glows in the dark | Because it always has six arms | Because it lives in the sky
test: Where does a starfish usually live? | In the desert sand | High in the sky | In tall trees | *On the sea floor and on rocks
test: Which word is another name for starfish? | Sea shell | Sea fish | Sea urchin | *Sea star
exam: Which statement is true? | A starfish is a bird that lives on rocks | *A starfish is a sea animal with no backbone, and it is not a fish | A starfish is a fish with a backbone | A starfish is a star in the night sky
